    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.811"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    dct:type "resolution-route/computation" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.87"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "The systems are finite-description programs and their claimed prevalence can be directly estimated or enumerated. Existing computation can resolve bounded horizons and frequencies, but not prove unrestricted randomness for all qualifying trajectories." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Enumerate the stated local rewiring-rule classes, run each from standardized initial networks, and classify node-count series for repetition, nesting, and statistical irregularity. Estimate the fraction of distance-two rules meeting preregistered randomness criteria and test the restricted-class repetition assertion." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Apparent randomness is test-dependent.", "Long transients can masquerade as nonrepetition.", "The exact rule grammar and equivalence classes affect the one-in-10,000 frequency." .
